{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>He who walks, etc.</b> These are the words of the prophet. For he who walks righteousness, and the word is missing a bet." "<b>Who shuts.</b> Closes, like יאטם אזנו (Psalms 58:5). And if they are two binyanim:" "<b>And shuts.</b> Like ויעצם את עיניכם (Isaiah 29:10). And if they are two binyanim:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:30.424643022Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}